  "notes": "West leads the ♥K against 3♦. West's ♥K wins the first trick and he continues with the ♥A and the ♥Q. East makes the fine play of ruffing his partner's winning heart with the ♦10. If South is not careful he will eventually lose a diamond trick and 2 club tricks and the contract will fail.\n\nSuppose South makes the natural-looking play of overruffing the ♦10 with the ♦A or ♦K. 2 rounds of trump reveal that a trump trick has been promoted for West. South will be able to get rid of one of his club losers on dummy's spades, but he will still have no way to avoid losing 2 club tricks.\n\nSouth can guard against this danger by discarding a club loser instead of overruffing East's ♦10. East will return a club, but South can win the ♣A and draw 3 rounds of trump. North's spades will take care of another club loser, leaving only 1 club trick to be lost at the end.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♥K against 3♦. West's ♥K wins the first trick and he continues with the ♥A and the ♥Q. East makes the fine play of ruffing his partner's winning heart with the ♦10. If South is not careful he will eventually lose a diamond trick and 2 club tricks and the contract will fail.",
    "Suppose South makes the natural-looking play of overruffing the ♦10 with the ♦A or ♦K. 2 rounds of trump reveal that a trump trick has been promoted for West. South will be able to get rid of one of his club losers on dummy's spades, but he will still have no way to avoid losing 2 club tricks.",
    "South can guard against this danger by discarding a club loser instead of overruffing East's ♦10. East will return a club, but South can win the ♣A and draw 3 rounds of trump. North's spades will take care of another club loser, leaving only 1 club trick to be lost at the end."
